From: Bruno Verachten <gounthar@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: build the Xen accelerator on riscv64 hosts

Xen targets are only listed for x86, arm and aarch64 hosts, so a
riscv64 build with --enable-xen silently has no Xen support. Use the
i386 emulator for its xenpv machine, as on arm, so qemu-system-i386
-M xenpv can serve PV backends (xenfb/vkbd) in a riscv64 dom0.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Verachten <gounthar@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -320,6 +320,9 @@
 elif cpu == 'aarch64'
   # i386 emulator provides xenpv machine type for multiple architectures
   xen_targets = ['i386-softmmu', 'x86_64-softmmu', 'aarch64-softmmu']
+elif cpu == 'riscv64'
+  # i386 emulator provides xenpv machine type for multiple architectures
+  xen_targets = ['i386-softmmu']
 else
   xen_targets = []
 endif
